<script lang="ts">
	import { englishExamples as examples } from '../../utils/examples.en'
	const count = signal(0)
	const actions = signal(0)
	const iconClicks = signal(0)
	const pinned = signal(false)
	const copies = signal(0)
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Button"
		description="Run an action, open a URL or navigate to a route with a single visual API."
	>
		<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UIButton on:click="() => count.value++">Save change</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="surface"
				color="neutral"
			>
				Secondary
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="outline"
				color="neutral"
			>
				Outline
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="ghost"
				color="neutral"
			>
				Ghost
			</UIButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<p role="status">Changes in this example: {count.value}</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.button" />
		<h2 id="appearance">Appearance</h2>
		<p>
			The look combines a treatment,
			<code>variant</code>
			(<code>solid</code>,
			<code>soft</code>, <code>surface</code>, <code>outline</code>, <code>subtle</code>,
			<code>ghost</code>
			or
			<code>link</code>), with a semantic color,
			<code>color</code>
			(<code>primary</code>,
			<code>secondary</code>, <code>neutral</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>info</code>,
			<code>warning</code>
			or
			<code>danger</code>). Without them it is
			<code>solid</code>
			and
			<code>primary</code>.
			<code>size</code>
			goes from
			<code>xs</code>
			to
			<code>xl</code>,
			<code>radius</code>
			from
			<code>none</code>
			to
			<code>full</code>, and
			<code>width="full"</code>
			and
			<code>elevation</code>
			complete the catalog. It is the
			<code>buttonTheme</code>
			recipe of
			<code>@meekojs/ui/theme</code>: your
			<code>class</code>
			is merged with Tailwind Merge and wins over the utility of the recipe that sets the same property.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UIButton
				variant="solid"
				color="primary"
				size="lg"
				radius="full"
				elevation="sm"
			>
				Save
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="soft"
				color="success"
				size="sm"
			>
				Publish
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="outline"
				color="info"
			>
				outline
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="ghost"
				color="primary"
			>
				ghost
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="link"
				color="primary"
			>
				link
			</UIButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.buttonAppearance" />
		<h2 id="kinds">Route, link or button</h2>
		<p>
			<code>UIButton</code>
			renders the element that matches what it does, with the same look: with
			<code>to</code>, a link to a route of the application that navigates without reloading; with <code>href</code>, an
			<code>&lt;a&gt;</code>
			to any URL; with neither, a
			<code>&lt;button type="button"&gt;</code>.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview id="button-kinds">
			<UIButton
				id="button-kind-route"
				to="/links"
				on:click="() => actions.value++"
			>
				See links
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				id="button-kind-anchor"
				href="https://github.com/meekojs/meeko"
				target="_blank"
				on:click="() => actions.value++"
			>
				GitHub
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				id="button-kind-button"
				on:click="() => actions.value++"
			>
				Action
			</UIButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<p
			id="button-kinds-status"
			role="status"
		>
			Clicks on these three: {actions.value}
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.buttonKinds" />
		<p>
			Combinations that make no sense are type errors in
			<code>meeko check</code>
			and in the editor:
			<code>to</code>
			with
			<code>href</code>,
			<code>type</code>
			or
			<code>disabled</code>
			on a link,
			<code>target</code>
			on a button, a route that does not exist or a dynamic route without
			<code>params</code>. A link cannot be disabled: it has no native state, and
			<code>aria-disabled</code>
			without removing
			<code>href</code>
			would still navigate. If the action is not available, do not render the link, or use a button with
			<code>disabled</code>.
		</p>
		<h2 id="sizes">Sizes and states</h2>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UIButton size="xs">Tiny</UIButton>
			<UIButton size="sm">Small</UIButton>
			<UIButton size="md">Medium</UIButton>
			<UIButton size="lg">Large</UIButton>
			<UIButton size="xl">Huge</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				radius="full"
				variant="outline"
				color="neutral"
			>
				Round
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton disabled>Unavailable</UIButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<h2 id="tone">Danger, loading and icon</h2>
		<p>
			<code>color="danger"</code>
			marks a destructive action, with any variant.
			<code>loading</code>
			keeps the text, adds the spinner, announces
			<code>aria-busy</code>
			and blocks the action without taking its focus. With
			<code>iconOnly</code>, the button is square: always name it with <code>ariaLabel</code>.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UIButton color="danger">Delete</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				color="danger"
				variant="outline"
			>
				Revoke
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton bind:loading="true">Saving</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				iconOnly
				ariaLabel="Delete"
				variant="outline"
				color="neutral"
			>
				<UIIcon name="lucide:trash-2" />
			</UIButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.buttonStates" />
		<DocsApi
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'to', type: 'RouteId', description: 'A route of the application. Renders a link that navigates without reloading. Excludes href, type and disabled.' },
				{ name: 'params / search', type: 'route params / object', description: 'With to: the params of a dynamic route (required there) and the query string.' },
				{ name: 'href', type: 'string', description: 'Any URL. Renders an <a>. Excludes to, type and disabled.' },
				{ name: 'target / rel / download', type: 'string', description: 'With to or href. For _blank, noopener noreferrer is added when rel is not set.' },
				{ name: 'type', type: 'button | submit | reset', default: 'button', description: 'Without to or href. Native behavior in forms.' },
				{ name: 'disabled', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Without to or href. Disables the native button.' },
				{ name: 'variant', type: 'solid | soft | surface | outline | subtle | ghost | link', default: 'solid', description: 'Visual treatment of the action.' },
				{ name: 'color', type: 'primary | secondary | neutral | success | info | warning | danger', default: 'primary', description: 'Semantic color; danger marks a destructive action.' },
				{ name: 'size', type: 'xs | sm | md | lg | xl', default: 'md', description: 'Size of the control.' },
				{ name: 'radius', type: 'none | xs | sm | md | lg | xl | 2xl | 3xl | full', default: 'md', description: 'Radius of the outline.' },
				{ name: 'width / elevation', type: 'auto | full / none … 2xl', description: 'Width of the content or of the container, and shadow.' },
				{ name: 'loading', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Adds the spinner, announces aria-busy and blocks the action without taking its focus.' },
				{ name: 'iconOnly / ariaLabel', type: 'boolean / string', default: 'false', description: 'A square button with an icon; ariaLabel gives its accessible name.' },
				{ name: 'name / value / form', type: 'string', description: 'Without to or href. The native attributes of a submit button.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes, merged with Tailwind Merge: they win over those of the recipe.' },
				{ name: 'id / title / aria-* / data-*', type: 'HTML attributes', description: 'Reach the element as they are.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="events">Events and content</h2>
		<p>
			<code>on:click</code>
			receives the mouse event in all three forms; on a link,
			<code>event.preventDefault()</code>
			cancels the navigation. The
			<code>default</code>
			snippet is required. For an asynchronous action, bind
			<code>loading</code>
			to your signal.
		</p>
		<p>
			For a link with its own visual hierarchy and the defaults of
			<code>ui.defaults.link</code>, use <MeekoLink to="/links">UILink</MeekoLink>.
		</p>
		<h2 id="icon-button">UIIconButton</h2>
		<p>
			An icon-only action with the three forms of
			<code>UIButton</code>
			(<code>to</code>,
			<code>href</code>
			or a button) and the same look (<code>variant</code>, but
			<code>link</code>, <code>color</code>, <code>size</code>,
			<code>radius</code>
			and
			<code>elevation</code>), square and
			<code>ghost</code>
			and
			<code>neutral</code>
			by default.
			<code>label</code>
			is required: it is its accessible name and the text of its tooltip, which is not announced again as a description. The icon is
			<code>icon</code>, the name of an icon of the package or the stroke of a 16 by 16 <code>&lt;path&gt;</code>, or your own
			<code>&lt;svg aria-hidden="true"&gt;</code>
			in the snippet. It is phrasing content: it fits inside a paragraph or a toolbar.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview id="icon-buttons">
			<UIIconButton
				id="icon-button-menu"
				label="Open the menu"
				icon="menu"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Close"
				icon="close"
				variant="outline"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Confirm"
				icon="check"
				variant="solid"
				color="primary"
				on:click="() => iconClicks.value++"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Languages"
				icon="globe"
				variant="surface"
				radius="full"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="See links"
				icon="arrowEnd"
				to="/links"
			/>
			<UIIconButton label="Delete">
				<UIIcon name="lucide:trash-2" />
			</UIIconButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<p
			id="icon-button-status"
			role="status"
		>
			Confirmations: {iconClicks.value}
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.iconButton" />
		<h3 id="icon-button-states">Toggle, danger, loading and sizes</h3>
		<p>
			With
			<code>pressed</code>, a button is a toggle: it renders
			<code>aria-pressed</code>
			and the active look. A link does not take it.
			<code>tooltip="false"</code>
			removes the tooltip when the context already explains the action; the name is still
			<code>label</code>.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview id="icon-button-states-preview">
			<UIIconButton
				id="icon-button-pin"
				label="Pin the panel"
				icon="check"
				variant="outline"
				bind:pressed="pinned.value"
				on:click="() => (pinned.value = !pinned.value)"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Remove"
				icon="close"
				color="danger"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Remove all"
				icon="close"
				color="danger"
				variant="solid"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Saving"
				icon="check"
				variant="surface"
				bind:loading="true"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Archive (unavailable)"
				icon="check"
				variant="surface"
				disabled
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Small"
				icon="menu"
				size="sm"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="Large"
				icon="menu"
				size="lg"
			/>
			<UIIconButton
				label="No tooltip"
				icon="menu"
				bind:tooltip="false"
			/>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.iconButtonStates" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIIconButton props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', description: 'Required. Accessible name and text of the tooltip.' },
				{ name: 'icon', type: 'UIIconName | string', description: 'An icon of the package (close, menu, check, info…) or the d stroke of a 16 by 16 path. Without it, the default snippet.' },
				{ name: 'tooltip', type: 'boolean', default: 'true', description: 'With false, no tooltip.' },
				{ name: 'placement', type: 'PopoverPlacement', default: 'top', description: 'Where the tooltip opens.' },
				{ name: 'pressed', type: 'boolean', description: 'Without to or href. A toggle: renders aria-pressed and the active look.' },
				{ name: 'to / params / search / href / target / rel / download', type: 'as in UIButton', description: 'A route or a link.' },
				{ name: 'type / disabled', type: 'button | submit | reset / boolean', default: 'button / false', description: 'Without to or href. The native button.' },
				{ name: 'variant', type: 'solid | soft | surface | outline | subtle | ghost', default: 'ghost', description: 'Visual treatment.' },
				{ name: 'color', type: 'primary | secondary | neutral | success | info | warning | danger', default: 'neutral', description: 'Semantic color; danger marks a destructive action.' },
				{ name: 'size / radius / elevation', type: 'xs … xl / none … full / none … 2xl', default: 'md / md', description: 'Size, radius of the outline and shadow.' },
				{ name: 'loading', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Swaps the icon for the spinner, announces aria-busy and blocks the action.' },
				{ name: 'class / ui', type: 'string / { base, icon, tooltip }', description: 'Classes of the button and of its parts.' },
			]"
		/>
		<h2 id="copy-button">UICopyButton</h2>
		<p>
			Copies
			<code>value</code>
			to the clipboard. With text it looks like
			<code>UIButton</code>
			(<code>surface</code>
			and
			<code>neutral</code>
			by default) and its text turns into “Copied” for a moment; with
			<code>iconOnly</code>, like <code>UIIconButton</code>, with its tooltip, and the icon turns into a check mark. The result is announced in a
			<code>role="status"</code>
			region and comes with the
			<code>copy</code>
			and
			<code>copyError</code>
			events. Without JavaScript it cannot copy: it waits hidden, without moving anything, until the page hydrates.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview id="copy-buttons">
			<UICopyButton
				id="copy-button-text"
				value="pnpm add @meekojs/ui"
				on:copy="() => copies.value++"
			/>
			<UICopyButton
				value="https://ui.meekojs.com"
				label="Copy link"
				variant="outline"
				size="sm"
			/>
			<UICopyButton
				id="copy-button-icon"
				value="sk_test_4f8a"
				iconOnly
				label="Copy the token"
				on:copy="() => copies.value++"
			/>
		</DocsPreview>
		<p
			id="copy-button-status"
			role="status"
		>
			Copies in this example: {copies.value}
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.copyButton" />
		<p>
			The texts come from the
			<code>copyButton.copy</code>,
			<code>copyButton.copied</code>
			and
			<code>copyButton.failed</code>
			messages (see <MeekoLink to="/theming">Theming</MeekoLink>), and the props win over them. On a solid background the text keeps its color; in the other variants, the result takes its tokens:
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="CSS"
			bind:code="examples.copyButtonTokens"
		/>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UICopyButton props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'value', type: 'string', description: 'Required. The text to copy.' },
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', default: 'Copy', description: 'Text of the button; with iconOnly, its accessible name and its tooltip.' },
				{ name: 'copiedLabel / failedLabel', type: 'string', default: 'Copied / Could not copy', description: 'Text and announcement of the result.' },
				{ name: 'iconOnly', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Icon only, with the look of UIIconButton.' },
				{ name: 'tooltip / placement', type: 'boolean / PopoverPlacement', default: 'true / top', description: 'With iconOnly, the tooltip.' },
				{ name: 'variant', type: 'solid | soft | surface | outline | subtle | ghost', default: 'surface; ghost with iconOnly', description: 'Visual treatment.' },
				{ name: 'color / size / radius', type: 'primary … danger / xs … xl / none … full', default: 'neutral / md / md', description: 'Semantic color, size and radius.' },
				{ name: 'disabled', type: 'boolean', default: 'false', description: 'Disables the native button.' },
				{ name: 'on:copy / on:copyError', type: '(value: string) / (error: unknown)', description: 'After copying, with the copied text, or when the copy fails.' },
				{ name: 'class / ui', type: 'string / { base, status }', description: 'Classes of the button and of the screen reader announcement.' },
			]"
		/>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
